  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Iron ore is one of the most common and valuable resources found on Earth,
    forming the backbone of human tools, machines, and construction. It appears naturally
    as reddish, brown, or dark gray rock and is packed with iron rich minerals like
    hematite and magnetite. Iron ore is abundant in the Earth\u2019s crust and often
    found in large deposits created by ancient geological processes, making it one
    of the easiest metals to locate and mine. Despite its plain appearance, this
    ore is incredibly important once smelted, it becomes strong and versatile iron,
    used to craft weapons, tools, buildings, vehicles, and nearly everything in modern
    technology."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
